 - The `users` array contains the current page of results; if there are more users, follow the `Link` response header with `rel="next"`
 
 To change who has access, use `PUT /:account_slug/boards/:board_id` with the `user_ids` parameter.
+
+## Publish a board
+
+```
+POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication
+```
+
+Publishes a board for read-only access by anyone with its secret public URL. Only
+account admins (including owners) who can access the board can publish it. Returns
+`204 No Content`. Repeated requests keep the same public URL.
+
+Board JSON includes `public_url`: `null` when unpublished, or an absolute URL such
+as `https://app.fizzy.do/public/boards/SECRET_KEY` when published. Public links do
+not require authentication or an account slug. Draft cards are never exposed.
+
+Public pages are available at:
+
+- `/public/boards/:key`
+- `/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Columns and cards must belong to the board identified by the key.
+
+## Unpublish a board
+
+```
+DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication
+```
+
+Revokes the board's public URL, including direct links to its columns and cards.
+Only account admins (including owners) who can access the board can unpublish it.
+Returns `204 No Content`, including when the board is already unpublished.
+Publishing again generates a new secret URL; old URLs remain invalid.
diff --git a/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cc4206d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+require "test_helper"
+
+class Boards::PublicationsControllerTest < ActionDispatch::IntegrationTest
+  setup do
+    sign_in_as :kevin
+    @board = boards(:writebook)
+  end
+
+  test "admins can publish and unpublish a board" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_response :no_content
+    assert @board.reload.published?
+
+    get board_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_equal public_board_url(@board.publication.key, script_name: nil), response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+
+    delete board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert_response :no_content
+    assert_not @board.reload.published?
+
+    get board_path(@board), as: :json
+    assert response.parsed_body.key?("public_url")
+    assert_nil response.parsed_body["public_url"]
+  end
+
+  test "publishing and unpublishing are idempotent" do
+    2.times do
+      post board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_response :no_content
+      @key ||= @board.reload.publication.key
+      assert_equal @key, @board.reload.publication.key
+    end
+
+    2.times do
+      delete board_publication_path(@board), as: :json
+      assert_response :no_content
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "HTML publication actions redirect to board settings" do
+    post board_publication_path(@board)
+    assert_redirected_to edit_board_path(@board)
+
+    delete board_publication_path(@board)
+    assert_redirected_to edit_board_path(@board)
+  end
+
